meta {
  name: Group events (realtime — transport TBD)
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/khatm/groups/:groupId/events
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  groupId: uuid
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Replaces: the Supabase Realtime postgres_changes subscription in
  useKhatmQueries.useKhatmRealtime (src ~lines 202-258). Transport is Zia's
  call — this file documents what the client consumes today.

  The client needs, per group, while the dashboard is open:
  1. "something changed on khatm_juz_assignments for this group"
     → it invalidates and refetches the dashboard (no payload needed beyond
       the signal itself)
  2. "group status became COMPLETED"
     → it navigates to the celebration screen
  3. connection state (SUBSCRIBED vs error/timeout)
     → drives a "Reconnecting…" banner

  Proposal: SSE on this endpoint emitting
    event: assignments-changed   data: {}
    event: group-completed       data: { "group_id": "uuid" }

  Accepted v1 fallback: no realtime endpoint at all — the client's TanStack
  Query staleTime is already 10s; switching the dashboard to
  refetchInterval polling degrades gracefully. If polling is chosen, the
  reconnect banner and instant completion navigation are lost; completion can
  be detected from the polled group.status instead.

  Authorization: members only.
}
